1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,000
The launch date just slipped. Where on the Moon do you land now?

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Tell it where, when and what matters.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Sun and Earth, checked against the real LOLA horizon.
Time-lapse of the real computation.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,000
160,000 km², hour by hour. Scored in 15 s, in the browser.
Measured: 14.8 s on 4 CPU cores, no GPU.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,800
The best site, with its best landing window.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,000
Sunlight left. Next night. When the Earth sets.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Side by side with the Artemis III candidate regions.

8
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:21,600
Then walk the site at 1:1 scale.
LOLA 240 m relief. Smaller craters and rocks are generated.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,500
South Pole. North Pole. Whole Moon.

10
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:28,000
Checked against JPL Horizons: within 0.002 arcminutes.
Sun and Earth azimuth and elevation, 726 comparisons at 3 sites.

11
00:00:28,067 --> 00:00:30,000
Mare Hackematis, by Hackemate. NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026.
